      },
      "methodTier": "tier 2",
      "methodModelDescription": "The Irish national GHG inventory (Duffy et al., 2014) was followed to estimate CH4 emission from ruminants and manure. Enteric CH4 loss for ewes, hoggets and rams was estimated as 6.5% of gross energy intake (GEI) depending on the digestibility of the diet. For lambs, no enteric CH4 emission were estimated for the first month post lambing, because milk was largely sufficient to sustain lamb growth. From week 5, enteric CH4 emission was estimated as 6% of lambs GEI.",
      "@type": "Emission"
    }
